<AppLayout title="Erawan terms of service" description="Terms for using Erawan: your files, connected services, and the MIT software licence.">
<div class="e-terms">
<p class="e-back"><a href="/apps/erawan/">← Erawan</a> · <a href="/apps/erawan/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p>
<h1>Erawan terms of service</h1>
<p class="e-date">Last updated 13 November 2026</p>
<p>Erawan is software you run on your own computer to back up files, compare and consolidate folders, and find duplicates. It is under active development. Erawan does not provide hosted backup storage or an Erawan account.</p>
<h2>Your files and choices</h2>
<p>You retain your rights in your files. Using Erawan does not give its authors ownership of them. Use the program only with files, accounts and systems you are authorised to access.</p>
<p>You choose the sources, destinations and operations. Review the selected paths, options and proposed actions before proceeding. Copying, consolidating, linking and deleting can change files or remove copies. Keep independent backups of important data and test that you can restore them.</p>
<p>Read each job's verification result and any errors. A verification result describes the checks performed for that job; it is not a guarantee of future file integrity or that every restore will succeed.</p>
<h2>Connected services</h2>
<p>When you connect storage or a server, its provider's terms, limits and charges apply separately. You are responsible for the accounts, credentials and API clients you configure, and for storage, transfer or API charges incurred through them. Erawan's authors do not operate those services.</p>
<p>Google Drive sign-in is handled by Google and rclone. The Drive backup-source setup requests read-only access. You can revoke access through your Google account and remove the local remote configuration; the <a href="/apps/erawan/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains how.</p>
<h2>Software licence and warranty</h2>
<p>Erawan's software and accompanying documentation are licensed under the MIT License below. These usage notes do not replace or restrict that licence. Third-party software used with Erawan is covered by its own licences. Erawan is provided as is, without a promised support service or availability commitment.</p>
